# {{name}}

A [Lanes](https://github.com/tacitresearch/lanes) application.

```bash
lake exe cache get      # once: prebuilt Mathlib
lake build
lake test               # model checks
lake exe {{name}} 8080  # run
```

## Lanes rules for agents

- Read LANES_STYLE.md before writing code. Cite rule numbers in PR descriptions when a rule shaped a choice.
- Write or update the spec first; model-check it before writing the implementation or a proof.
- step is pure: no IO. New external work = new Effect constructor + response message.
- Encode invariants in types first, theorems second, runtime asserts only at adapters.
- Never add sorry, partial, unsafe or an axiom without listing it in TRUSTED.md.
- On an unexpected state, emit stop; do not add defensive fallbacks.
- Run `lanes lint && lake test` before claiming a task is done.

## Layout

- `{{Name}}/Counter.lean`: logic. The spec, the actor and its invariant. Pure: no IO.
- `{{Name}}/Proofs.lean`: proofs that need `Lanes.Semantics`, such as refinement to the spec.
- `Check.lean`: model checks on small instances, run by `lake test`.
- `Main.lean`: the edge. HTTP, HTML views, `main`.

Executable code imports `Lanes`. Proof files that need refinement or Mathlib import
`Lanes.Semantics`; keep that import out of anything `Main.lean` depends on, or the binary grows
by over 100 MB.
